Advanced Technologies Project 1 - Immersive Learning in AR

Introduction
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This application is an AR Mobile system built for iOS and Android. It showcases a range of
physics based systems such as Atomic Structures and Radiation

How to Run (PC)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Open the project in Unity version 6000.1.9f1
2. Run the program in sample scene
3. Controls are right mouse button to select, right and left mouse button to rotate with selected object,
mouse wheel to scale and right clicking into blank space deselects objects

If you encounter texture errors from an Engine Conversion

1. Navigate to Window/Rendering/PipelineConverter
2. Tick the top 2 options and run the conversion
3. Then navigate to the Settings Folder in Assets and Add a background render feature to each forward renderer

How to Run (iOS)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Set build profile to iOS, ensure you select Developer Mode
2. Add anything to the Camera reference in player settings
3. Build the project onto a Macbook so Xcode will automatically run
4. When Xcode launches
	a. Enable automatic signing
	b. Have a development team set up
	c. Ensure you connect an apple device (iPhone) to the mac which is part of that developer team
	d. Go to Frame work and iLinker flags and delete both -iWeakSystem and -64 from all flags
	e. Run the Xcode project

How to Run (Android)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Set Build profile to Andriod
2. Build to correct Android version
3. Take the created APK file and run it on you phone
